Harrow, once called Leitmotif, is a [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessian]] of the first generation, and [[Org/Sedecium|Sedecium]] calls it the God Eater. It set out to take the life and abilities of other Thessians into itself, and took a new name when it began killing them. It has killed at least one of the good Thessians; [[People/Althane/The Broker|the Broker]] was present when it happened and took part of that one's portfolio rather than let the Harrow swallow it whole, and the Harrow got the knowledge out of the kill.

The Harrow is barely conscious now, not much more than a bundle of want, and goes on killing Thessians and taking what they hold. Where it feeds it is attended by a brood: a vast yellow cloud of creatures that hangs over the body and breaks off in numbers to fall on anything near. One seen closely was the length of a man, yellow-skinned, and almost nothing but mouth, the front of it a wide open maw with a second jaw set crosswise inside and a long tail trailing behind, flying with no wings. It killed [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/Tithe|Tithe]], a Thessian the size of a planet, and settled in to devour the body. Its work is no direct threat to most of the Astra so far. In the near term it thins the Thessians; in the long run it grows.
